---
import Shell from '../../../layouts/Shell.astro';
import study from '../../../../../../kb/research/references/data/osha-culture.json';
import navigation from '../../../../../../kb/research/references/data/osha-seasonal-navigation.json';
import {timingTokens, timingLabel} from '../../../lib/osha-navigation.mjs';
const byProfile=new Map(navigation.rows.map(row=>[row.profile_id,row]));
---
<Shell title="Osha, stories & the food year" description="Explore Odisha’s osha, brata and parba through their stories, seasons, household practices and food." active="explore" related={false}>
<div class="wrap">
<header class="osha-cover">
<p class="eyebrow">Living traditions · A continuing collection</p>
<p class="saying">Bara masa, tera parba</p>
<h1>A year of stories.<br/><em>A place at the table.</em></h1>
<p class="lead">Follow Odisha’s osha, brata and parba through a grain offering, a knotted thread, a leaf-wrapped pitha—and the stories people tell around them.</p>
<p>Some occasions gather a family around food. Others give meaning to restraint. Begin with an observance, then discover the story and the questions still worth asking.</p>
<a href="#observances" class="utk-button">Explore the observances ↓</a>
</header>
<section class="osha-intro" aria-labelledby="read-the-year"><h2 id="read-the-year">More than a festival menu</h2><p>Food can carry a memory of hunger, a hope for a child, or a question about who is welcome to eat. These pages bring ritual narratives, documented accounts and food practices into conversation. Regional and household differences remain part of the story.</p><p class="note">This collection has {study.pages.filter(p=>p.coverage_status==='narrative_checkpoint').length} narrative checkpoints and {study.pages.filter(p=>p.coverage_status==='research_note').length} early research notes. Histories and local accounts are still being developed. Traditional months help you explore; they are not confirmed event dates. Where sources disagree about a month or identity, use “Month or identity unresolved”. Recurring vows and Raja’s solar transition have their own groups.</p></section>
<section id="observances" class="osha-list" aria-labelledby="collection-title"><p class="eyebrow">Stories across the year</p><h2 id="collection-title">Where would you like to begin?</h2>
<form class="osha-filters" role="search" onsubmit="return false"><label>Find an observance or food<input id="osha-search" type="search" placeholder="Try enduri, khuda or Lakshmi"/></label><label>Month or recurrence<select id="osha-month"><option value="">All timings</option>{navigation.months.map(m=><option value={"month:"+m.id}>{m.label}</option>)}<option value="recurring">Recurring observances</option><option value="unresolved">Month or identity unresolved</option><option value="solar">Solar transition</option></select></label><button id="osha-reset" type="reset">Show all</button></form>
<p id="osha-count" role="status" aria-live="polite">{study.pages.length} observances</p>
<div class="osha-grid">{study.pages.map(p=>{const entry=byProfile.get(p.id);return <article class="osha-card" data-profile-id={p.id} data-timings={timingTokens(entry).join(" ")} data-search={[p.name,p.lead,...p.food_names,...p.sections.map(s=>s.text)].join(' ').toLowerCase()}><p class="eyebrow">{timingLabel(entry,navigation.months)} · {p.observance_type}</p><h3><a href={p.route}>{p.name} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3><p>{p.lead}</p><details class="timing-note"><summary>About this timing</summary><p>{entry.calendar_note}</p></details><p class="food-line">{p.food_names.length?p.food_names.join(' · '):'Food association still being researched'}</p><p class="food-role">{entry.food_role_note}</p><p class="reading-stage">{p.coverage_status==='narrative_checkpoint'?'Story & food checkpoint':'Early notes · history incomplete'}</p></article>})}</div><p id="osha-empty" hidden>No match in this first collection. Try another food or show all timings.</p>
</section>
<section class="osha-next"><div><p class="eyebrow">From reading to a visit</p><h2>Ask about the food.<br/><em>Listen for the story.</em></h2></div><div><p>Use the collection to find something you would like to learn about. Ask a cook which version they make, what the occasion means to them and whether it is available during your visit.</p><p>No serving place or current event date is confirmed here. A food sale and an invitation to private worship are different arrangements.</p><p><a href="/culture/osha/finding-seasonal-food/">Read a food notice before planning a visit →</a></p><a href="/food/">Explore food & flavours →</a></div></section>
<section class="osha-research"><p><a href="/culture/osha/which-osha/">Which Osha? Find the right full-moon tradition →</a></p><h2>The next chapters</h2><p>We are tracing Odia katha editions and local histories, and extending regional accounts. Chaitra Mangala, Sathi and Nisha Mangalabara now have initial profiles. Pua Jiuntia, Bhai Jiuntia and Nuakhai now offer western Odisha reading routes. Bata, Pandu and Shani/Tota add further accounts of vows, offerings and recurring observances. The expanded collection keeps local practices, textual comparisons and unresolved food identities distinct. Further textual and regional research remains open. It is a research path, not a claim to have covered every observance.</p><a href="/contribute/">Share a source or suggest a correction →</a></section>
<details class="osha-evidence"><summary>About the research</summary><p>Prepared with AI assistance under the direction of Ahimanikya Satapathy. Sources checked 7–10 October 2026; no local interviews or human factual review claimed. Each article links its sources and identifies unresolved claims. Legends are presented as narratives, not dated historical events.</p></details>
</div>
</Shell>
<script>
import {matchesNavigation} from '../../../lib/osha-navigation.mjs';
const field=document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#osha-search');
const month=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#osha-month');
const cards=[...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.osha-card')];
function filter(){const q=(field?.value||'').trim().toLocaleLowerCase();let count=0;for(const card of cards){const show=matchesNavigation(card.dataset.search||'',(card.dataset.timings||'').split(' '),q,month?.value||'');card.hidden=!show;if(show)count++;}document.querySelector('#osha-count')!.textContent=`${count} ${count===1?'observance':'observances'}`;document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#osha-empty')!.hidden=count!==0;}
field?.addEventListener('input',filter);month?.addEventListener('change',filter);document.querySelector('#osha-reset')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{field!.value='';month!.value='';filter();});
</script>
<style>
.osha-cover{padding:clamp(32px,6vw,84px) 0 48px;max-width:880px}.saying{color:var(--earth);font-size:21px;letter-spacing:.04em}.osha-cover h1{font-size:clamp(44px,6.2vw,80px);line-height:1.07;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:25px 0}.osha-cover em,.osha-next em{color:var(--earth);font-weight:normal}.osha-cover .lead{font-size:clamp(22px,2.8vw,29px);line-height:1.55}.osha-cover>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:65ch}.osha-cover .utk-button{margin-top:20px}.osha-intro{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:38px 0;max-width:900px}.osha-intro h2,.osha-list h2,.osha-next h2,.osha-research h2{font-size:clamp(30px,3.4vw,44px);line-height:1.2}.osha-intro p,.osha-cover p,.osha-next p,.osha-research p{line-height:1.8}.note{padding:20px 24px;background:var(--paper);font-size:16px}.osha-list{scroll-margin-top:30px;padding-top:24px}.osha-filters{display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:end;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:32px 0 16px}.osha-filters label{display:grid;gap:8px;font-size:15px;flex:1;min-width:210px}.osha-filters input,.osha-filters select{font:inherit;padding:14px;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:3px;color:inherit;min-height:50px;width:100%}.osha-filters button{font:inherit;padding:14px 20px;background:transparent;border:1px solid var(--earth);color:var(--earth);cursor:pointer;min-height:50px}.osha-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:22px}.osha-card{padding:28px;background:var(--paper);border-top:3px solid var(--earth);display:flex;flex-direction:column}.osha-card[hidden]{display:none}.osha-card h3{font-size:29px;line-height:1.2;margin:16px 0}.osha-card h3 a{text-decoration:none}.osha-card h3 a:hover{text-decoration:underline}.osha-card p{line-height:1.7}.osha-card .food-line{font-size:15px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:16px;margin-top:auto}.food-role{font-size:14px}.timing-note{font-size:14px;margin-bottom:16px}.timing-note summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--earth)}.timing-note p{margin:10px 0}.reading-stage{font-size:13px;color:var(--earth)}.osha-next{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:50px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:64px;padding:40px 0}.osha-research{padding:28px;background:var(--paper);margin:25px 0}.osha-research p{max-width:80ch}.osha-evidence{font-size:15px;margin:32px 0}.osha-evidence p{max-width:80ch;line-height:1.7}a:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--earth);outline-offset:4px}@media(max-width:950px){.osha-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}@media(max-width:620px){.osha-grid,.osha-next{grid-template-columns:1fr}.osha-next{gap:10px}.osha-card{padding:23px}.osha-filters label{flex-basis:100%}.osha-filters button{width:100%}}
</style>
